    {
      "directNodeIds": [
        "cnm_200"
      ],
      "explanation": "Direct variation means \\(y=kx\\) for a fixed nonzero constant \\(k\\). Using \\(y=8\\) when \\(x=4\\),\n\\[\n8=4k,\\qquad k=2.\n\\]\nThus \\(y=2x\\), and when \\(x=-8\\),\n\\[\ny=2(-8)=-16.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{-16}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{A}}\\).",
      "id": "constant-of-variation",
      "sourceRef": "amc/1964_AMC_12_Q05#constant-of-variation",
      "title": "Find the constant multiplier"
    }
